# WanderPath — Project Context for AI Assistance

## What this is

WanderPath is a trip planner & local guide for **domestic travel inside
Iran** (e.g. Tehran → Shiraz, Mashhad → Yazd). **Google sign-in**
(accounts) replaces anonymous-only use for the main app; phone/SMS OTP is
**deferred** until an Iranian SMS provider is chosen (Kavenegar, Ghasedak,
MeliPayamak, etc.). No booking/payments, no AI assistant, no
reviews/ratings. Full RTL, Persian-first UI.

Read `docs/architecture-spec.md` first — it is the source of truth for
scope, module boundaries, and the API contract. Do not deviate from it
without discussing the tradeoff first (the spec's anonymous-auth section
is outdated; this file reflects the codebase).

## Routes (frontend)

- `/` — marketing landing page (Server Component hero + feature cards).
- `/login` — Google sign-in (`@react-oauth/google` → `POST /auth/google`).
- `/app` — trip list + create trip (auth required via `AuthGuard`).
- `/trip/[id]/*` — trip editor, summary (map), budget (auth required).

## Stack

- **Backend**: Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.0, Alembic, Pydantic
  v2, SQLite (dev) / PostgreSQL (prod)
- **Frontend**: Next.js 14 (App Router), TypeScript, React 18, plain
  CSS (no Tailwind/UI framework) — custom design system in
  `app/globals.css`

## Backend architecture — follow this strictly

Every module under `backend/app/modules/<name>/` follows:

```
Controller (router.py)  →  Service (service.py)  →  Repository (repository.py)
```

- **Repositories** (`repository.py`): pure DB access via SQLAlchemy.
  No business rules. No HTTP concerns.
- **Services** (`service.py`): all business logic and validation lives
  here. Ownership checks, domain rules, orchestration. Raises typed
  exceptions from `app/shared/exceptions.py` (`NotFoundError`,
  `OwnershipError`, `ValidationDomainError`, `ExternalProviderError`,
  `UnauthorizedError`) — never raises `HTTPException` directly.
- **Routers** (`router.py`): HTTP layer only. Parses request →
  calls service → returns response. No business logic.
- **DTOs** (`dtos.py`): Pydantic request/response schemas per module.
- **`dependencies.py`**: FastAPI DI wiring (composition root) for that
  module.

External integrations (Neshan APIs) are abstracted behind interfaces
so the provider can be swapped without touching domain code:

- `app/modules/destination/interfaces.py` → `IPlaceDataProvider`
- `app/modules/map/interfaces.py` → `IMapProvider`
- `app/modules/identity/interfaces.py` → `IIdentityResolver`
- Concrete implementations live in `app/infrastructure/providers/`

Caching policy (city/place data fetched from Neshan, persisted to the
DB, refreshed on staleness) lives in
`app/infrastructure/cache/place_cache_sync.py` — this is
infrastructure, not a service concern.

Driving distance/duration for destination search uses
`app/infrastructure/cache/route_distance_cache.py` (wraps
`IMapProvider.get_route`, keyed by rounded lat/lng, TTL in config).

Global exception handling is in `app/main.py`: `NotFoundError` → 404,
`OwnershipError` → 403, `UnauthorizedError` → 401,
`ValidationDomainError` → 422, `ExternalProviderError` → 503.

### Identity & ownership

- **`User` table** + **`app/modules/auth/`** — Google ID token verified
  server-side (`google-auth`); session JWT (`PyJWT`, `JWT_SECRET`).
- **`JwtIdentityResolver`** — reads `Authorization: Bearer <token>`,
  resolves to `User.id`.
- **`DeviceIdentityResolver`** — still present as **guest fallback**
  (`X-Device-Id` header) for legacy clients/tests during transition.
- **`get_current_device_id`** (in `identity/dependencies.py`): **JWT
  preferred** when Bearer present; otherwise device id. Comment in that
  file is authoritative.
- Trips still store **`owner_device_id`** (string) — now holds the
  authenticated user id for new trips. Column rename is deferred.
- **Anonymous trips are NOT migrated** to accounts in the current pass.

### Distance fields (Destination API)

- `GET /cities?q=...&trip_id=...` → optional
  `distance_from_origin_km` per city (haversine via `app/shared/geo.py`)
  when the trip has origin coordinates.
- `GET /cities/{id}/places?trip_id=...` → optional
  `distance_from_origin_km` + `duration_from_origin_minutes` per place
  (cached routing via `RouteDistanceCache`).

## Frontend architecture — follow this strictly

- `services/` — one thin wrapper per backend module (auth, destination,
  trip, budget, map, summary). All HTTP calls go through
  `services/apiClient.ts`, which sends `Authorization: Bearer` when a
  session token exists (`hooks/useAccessToken.ts`); falls back to
  `X-Device-Id` only when unauthenticated (guest/legacy).
- `hooks/useAccessToken.ts` — stores JWT from Google login.
- `hooks/useDeviceId.ts` — legacy guest device UUID (fallback only).
- `components/AuthGuard.tsx` — redirects `/app` and `/trip/*` to
  `/login` when no token.
- `modules/trip/localTrips.ts` — backend has **no** "list my trips"
  endpoint; frontend tracks trip ids in localStorage per browser.
- `modules/trip/placeCache.ts` — client-side cache of `Place` objects.
- `shared/types.ts` — TypeScript types mirroring backend DTOs.
- `shared/mapStyle.ts` — patches map styles for Persian labels; hides
  unreliable third-party place labels; trip pins show `pin.name` in UI.
  Two constraints the patch must keep: never emit `layout: undefined`
  (MapLibre validates the style object and refuses to render), and only
  rewrite `text-field` when it already reads a *name* — road shields read
  `ref` into a fixed-size icon and clip a long Persian name.
- Persian map labels need the RTL text plugin, or MapLibre draws them
  unshaped and reversed. It is vendored into `public/` by
  `scripts/copy-rtl-plugin.mjs` (runs on `predev`/`prebuild`) and enabled
  in `components/TripRouteMap.tsx`; self-hosted because CDNs are
  unreliable from Iran.
- `i18n/fa.ts` — all user-facing strings, not inline in components.
- `shared/format.ts` — Persian digits, Toman, distance/duration helpers.

## Design system

- Palette: deep indigo (`--ink-night`) for the header/hero band, warm
  parchment (`--paper`) for content, Persian-tile turquoise
  (`--turquoise`) as the primary interactive color, caravanserai
  terracotta (`--terracotta`) reserved for money/budget/warnings only.
- Type: Vazirmatn for all Persian text; **Space Mono only for
  numerals** (prices, counts, distances) — never mix.
- The itinerary's signature visual is the "route stitch" (`.route-
  stitch` / `.stop-marker` in `globals.css`) — preserve when editing
  `DayColumn.tsx`.
- Don't introduce Tailwind or a component library — extend
  `app/globals.css` with existing token variables.

## Current status / known gaps

- Backend: **87 tests** passing (`cd backend && pytest`).
- Frontend: builds cleanly (`npm run build`).
- **`GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`** / **`JWT_SECRET`** must be set for auth
  (`backend/.env`, `frontend/.env.local` — see `.env.example` files).
- **`NESHAN_API_KEY`** in `backend/.env` (service key). Direction returns HTTP **485** if that key’s service list does not include routing — provider then cools down and uses OSRM so the summary map does not stall. Map tiles still need a separate Neshan **web** key as `NEXT_PUBLIC_NESHAN_API_KEY` (optional; otherwise OpenFreeMap).
- Seed data covers major Iranian cities for demo without Neshan.
- Phone/SMS auth: **not implemented** — architecture ready via
  `IIdentityResolver`; pick provider later.
- Old anonymous trips (device-id ownership) are **not auto-linked** to
  new Google accounts.

## Working conventions

- Keep the Controller → Service → Repository split even for small
  features — don't shortcut business logic into a router.
- New business rules raise domain exceptions from
  `app/shared/exceptions.py`, not `HTTPException`.
- Any new backend module needs: `dtos.py`, `repository.py` (if DB),
  `service.py`, `dependencies.py`, `router.py`, registration in
  `app/main.py`.
- Any new frontend API call goes through a `services/*.ts` wrapper,
  typed against `shared/types.ts`.
- Write/update tests alongside backend changes (`backend/tests/`).
- Persian strings go in `i18n/fa.ts`, not inline.
